msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:256
#: b3152985782c4d15a0ec0175f915dd30
msgid "Linux Based Autopilots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:258
#: c114eb05112b4701be868c59481f7717
msgid "These autopilots use an underlying Linux OS. Linux boards usually have more CPU power and memory many of the other boards listed on this page, but do not support DShot, Bi-Directional DShot, BLHeli ESC passthrough, many of the ArduPilot GPIO based features, and easy upload from the ground stations. They do allow experimentation and development of advanced control and navigation algorithms (see also :ref:`common-companion-computers`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:272
#: cf46125ef8a54a40a964c15d0d68fbea
msgid "\\** these devices are sensor add-on boards for a Linux-based microcomputer. See board links for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:274
